Give the four Intent types the json factory and construct them through it

Dev accepted, in these words: "Accepted, build it" — the recommendation being that the four
Intent types, aerial FlightIntent, marine VoyageIntent, ethereal LaunchIntent and terrestrial
MarchIntent, take the json factory the four reports took: each a drake surface
`type X from <Medium> draco format dracon Dracon` with `factory parameters par json Json`, its JSON
re-canonicalized, its hand-written companion replaced by the generator's output, the eight test
sites that construct an intent as host text re-authored `X(payload)`, and one IntentFactoryTest
in the domains package with the three ReportFactoryTest cases iterating over the four.

Why the intents: they are each medium's entry message, the fact its OriginateReport joins, and
they were the one remaining shape of the kind the report thread repaired — derived from the medium
and Dracon, no elements, no factory, no drake surface, constructed only by tests, as
`new X { override lazy val typeDefinition …; override (lazy) val json = … }`. A Haskell target
needs their constructor as much as the reports'.

Probed before recommending, with the compiled CLIs on FlightIntent: the surface parses, emits back
clean, adds only the factory record to the JSON and 25 lines to the companion — `apply(_json: =>
Json)`, the Dracon-shaped encoder and decoder, `Null = apply(Json.Null)` — plus the two circe
imports, none removed. Built as probed over the four: four new drake surfaces, four JSON files
carrying the factory record and nothing else moved, four regenerated companions. `DrakeCLI check`
over aerial, marine, ethereal and terrestrial: surface drift 0, json drift 0 each. No engine
change, no definition site changed (no definition constructs an intent; Creator's messageType is
Dracon).

The eight test sites — the four OriginateReportTests (`override lazy val json = input`), the
marine, ethereal and terrestrial chain tests and AerialAssemblyTest (`override val json = payload`,
strict) — each lose their anonymous construction for the one-line call. The strict sites change
nothing observable: the payload at each is an already-built value, and the factory's by-name
binding captures an immutable Json, which also survives the actor boundary AerialAssemblyTest
sends it across.

IntentFactoryTest (3) is one suite, not four, because the four definitions are one pattern: each
case iterates over the four intents — exact trio agreement (emit, parse, generate, the factory's
one parameter named json typed Json, parents the medium then Dracon, the companion's loaded
definition equal to the file's); the by-name argument evaluated zero times until the first read
of `json`, once after, never again, the instance being its medium's type, Null's json being
Json.Null; and the codec round-trip for each (`asJson` is `{"json": payload}`, decoding reads the
intent back, an empty object decodes to Json.Null).

With this every message in the example chain — the four intents, the four reports and the World's
Location sink — constructs through its definition. The *Intent observation of the two report
records is closed; nothing from the report thread remains preserved.

